# Your data

The data that {{ project_name }} reads is yours, and it stays on this machine unless you send it somewhere. This page
says where each part is, what git keeps, and what leaves the machine. Fill in the rows for this app's sources.

## Where it is

| What | Where | In git? | Made again from |
|---|---|---|---|
| The source files | `data/` (this app's sources: say which) | no | where they came from |
| The database | `data/{{ db_file }}` (or `{{ env_prefix }}_DB`) | no | the source files{% if curations %} and `curated/`{% endif %} (`/ingest`) |
{%- if demo_data %}
| The demo database | `data/demo.duckdb` | no | `uv run {{ project_name }} demo` |
{%- endif %}
{%- if backup %}
| Backups | `backups/` (or `[backup] dir`), and Cloud Storage with `[backup] remote` | no | `uv run {{ project_name }} backup` |
{%- endif %}
| Settings and keys | `config.toml` | no | `config.example.toml`, and the services' consoles |
{%- if curations %}
| Curated decisions | `curated/*.csv` | **yes** | nothing: they are the backup of the decisions |
{%- endif %}

`.gitignore` keeps `data/`, `backups/`, every `*.duckdb` file and `config.toml` out of git. `privacy-check` (the
pre-commit hook) stops a commit that holds personal data.

**The source files are the record.** `ingest` only reads them. Keep a copy of them.

**The database can be made again** from the source files{% if curations %} and `curated/` (`/rebuild-database`){% else %} (`/ingest`){% endif %}{% if backup %}, or restored from a backup (`/restore-backup`){% endif %}.
{%- if curations %}

## What goes into git: `curated/`

The decisions that people or a model make cost time or money, so git keeps them (`curated/README.md` lists each
file). Each command that changes a decision writes the files again. The repo must stay private.
{%- endif %}

## What leaves the machine
{%- if not (motherduck or (curations and llm) or cloud_run or backup) %}

Nothing: no command sends the data anywhere.
{%- endif %}
{%- if backup %}

- **`backup`, with `[backup] remote`:** a copy of the whole database goes to your own Google Cloud Storage bucket,
  which must be private (`doctor --remote` checks).
{%- endif %}
{%- if motherduck %}
- **`publish`:** the contract's views go to MotherDuck (`md:{{ motherduck_db }}`), only when you run it. Only those
  views go, never the tables.
{%- endif %}
{%- if curations and llm %}
- **`classify`:** the text of the items to classify goes to Anthropic's API. It costs money, and the command says how
  much before a large run.
{%- endif %}
{%- if cloud_run %}
- **The hosted app** reads the MotherDuck copy, behind Google sign-in (`docs/guides/hosting.md`).
{%- endif %}
